Defconfigs this repository derives because the fork does not ship them, or ships them short of what a
fleet board needs. An external tree's config takes precedence over the fork's of the same name.

raspberrypi3_wpe_2_38_cog_defconfig is the fork's, plus what every bench system needs:

  BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT*               the board has no cable at the bench
  BR2_PACKAGE_OPENSSH (not DROPBEAR)        dropbear 2019.78 refuses ed25519 keys
  BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES    ../board/linux-fleet.fragment: TUN and netfilter
                                            for tailscale0
  BR2_PACKAGE_IPTABLES                      tailscaled's netfilter tool

raspberrypi3_wpe_2_46_cog_defconfig is the fork's 2.46 with the same four; against the 2.38 file it
differs only in what the release brings (BR2_PACKAGE_WPEWEBKIT2_46, gcc 11, WPEWEBKIT_USE_LIBWEBRTC=n),
so a 2.38-against-2.46 A/B compares releases.

The fork release-pins its cog defconfigs for the rpi3 only, so raspberrypi4_wpe_2_38_cog_defconfig is
the rpi3 2.38 one with the board changes taken from raspberrypi4_wpe_defconfig:

  BR2_cortex_a53 -> BR2_cortex_a72          the SoC
  no BR2_LINUX_KERNEL*                      the kernel is pinned (BR_KERNEL_DEB_URL)
  post-build.sh, post-image.sh, their args  board/raspberrypi4's
  RPI_FIRMWARE_VARIANT_PI4                  start4.elf/fixup4.dat, which genimage names
  RPI_FIRMWARE_3BPLUSNEW                    the fork's newest rpi-firmware (2023-03-06), which a
                                            rev 1.4/1.5 board boots; tree-patches/0002 lets the
                                            Pi 4 variant select it
  BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT*               as above
  BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2*                   the rpi3 2.38 defconfig emits a tarball only

Graphics: the Pi 4's VideoCore VI runs no vchiq GL service, so the rpi3's wpebackend-rdk on dispmanx
cannot render (measured 2026-08-31: every WPEWebProcess dies registering its vchiq service). The rpi4
stack is the fork's KMS one: wpebackend-fdo, cog's wayland platform, mesa v3d, weston on DRM, the
vc4-kms-v3d overlay, and python3 for the uinput seat shim; wpebackend-rdk is off so libwpe cannot
dlopen it as the default.

Kernel: the fork's rpi34-linux-5.15.config is a Pi 2/3 config (no MMC_SDHCI_IPROC, PCIE_BRCMSTB, XHCI,
LPAE or HIGHMEM; it hangs before init on an rpi4). RPi OS's gzip kernel7l 5.15.84 boots in 90 s
(measured 2026-08-31), so the profile pins that package and buildroot_ws.py installs its zImage and
device tree ahead of the board's post-image script.

TODO: a full bench run on the rpi4 2.38 image is unmeasured; its weston/mesa session has not yet drawn
a frame on the board.
